Interpretation rule:
- SPY is the primary passive opportunity-cost benchmark.
- RSP checks whether alpha is merely an equal-weight/smaller-stock effect.
- QQQ is a growth/tech opportunity-cost comparator.
- SMH is diagnostic only; it is NOT a fair primary benchmark unless the portfolio is semiconductor-dominated.
- Hit rate is descriptive, not an optimization target.
